-- title:
--   The initial 456-coordinate ray and its first image
-- statement:
--   Two literal arrays of natural numbers fix the candidate initial profile ray and its image under the unary phase. Each uses the common 456-coordinate ordering: four triangular blocks $A,B,M,C$, each with $78$ rank pairs $0\le i\le j<12$, followed by the $144$ ordered-pair entries of $W$.
--
--   These are exact integer profile values, interpreted as real upper bounds only when a scaling and semantic profile are applied. No numerical approximation enters their definitions.
